content.text:
Here’s what was going wrong and what we changed.

## Root cause

After the probe called `session.save` from the page, the **on-disk** session was correct (`persistedRowCount: 2`, etc.). On **window close**, `ShellContext` registers `beforeunload` / `pagehide` and runs **`flushPendingAutosave` → `saveActiveSession('flush')`**.

The session was still **unlocked** (`sessionPassphrasesRef` still had the passphrase from **Create session**). That flush wrote whatever was in **`chatLog`** — which never included the transcript you only wrote via **`window.api.session.save`** in `page.evaluate`. So the flush **re-saved an empty (or nearly empty) chat** and **wiped** the encrypted file. The relaunch probe then correctly saw `rowCount: 0`.

## Fix

Before closing the first app in the persistence scenario, **lock the active session** so `saveActiveSession` bails out and the flush cannot overwrite disk:

```196:203:C:\Users\KickA\Projects\Active\NeuralShell\tear\smoke-native-trust.js
    // beforeunload/pagehide flushes autosave; with an unlocked named session that saves in-memory
    // chat (often still empty vs the IPC-written transcript) and clobbers disk before exit.
    if (modeA.hasSessionModalFlow) {
      await pageA.getByTestId("lock-active-session-btn").click();
      await pageA.waitForTimeout(500);
    }

    await app.close();
```

With that, **`node tear/smoke-native-trust.js` exits 0** and `persistence_relaunch.pass` is **true** (session file size also went from ~520 bytes empty envelope to **684** with real transcript).

## Other changes already in play

- Synthetic transcript uses **`assistant`** instead of **`kernel`** so anything that only allows core roles cannot strip the proof line.
- Short **post-close delay**, **disk probe** in the report, **`waitForFunction`** on `window.api.session.load`, longer IPC retries, and optional **ipc probe** on failure.
- **`sessionManager`** now resolves the sessions directory via **`getSessionsDir()`** each time so it always tracks the current `userData` path (good after rebuilds).

The same lock-before-close logic is in your **`Documents\GitHub\NeuralShell`** copy of the smoke script as well. If you want this as a single commit, commit from **`C:\Users\KickA\Projects\Active\NeuralShell`** (that’s where the run succeeded).

[REDACTED]

